WEBVTT

00:23:28.473 --> 00:23:30.815
Stop talking about yourself so much."

00:23:30.839 --> 00:23:33.489
DB: Right. No, I do think,
I wouldn't say we raised,

00:23:33.513 --> 00:23:36.610
I think we're part of the generation
that is part of this problem.

00:23:36.634 --> 00:23:39.022
We've just buffered ourselves
from each other,

00:23:39.046 --> 00:23:41.401
partly over fear of intimacy.

00:23:41.425 --> 00:23:43.859
And so, the way you bring it back,

00:23:43.883 --> 00:23:45.933
sometimes it's through
formal organizations.

00:23:45.957 --> 00:23:49.423
One of the great weaver organizations
is called "Thread" in Baltimore.

00:23:49.447 --> 00:23:53.224
And there's a woman named Sarah Hemminger
who saw lonely kids in Baltimore,

00:23:53.248 --> 00:23:54.612
underperforming kids,

00:23:54.636 --> 00:23:58.475
so she surrounded them with four
sort of mentors who are volunteers,

00:23:58.499 --> 00:24:00.460
and then four more who are grandparents